content:
The `SplatMesh` is a regular Three.js object, so you can rotate it via `splat.rotation`. The cleanest way is to add an optional `splatRotation` field to the config:

**`src/channels/channelConfig.ts`** — add to the interface and each entry:
```typescript
export interface ChannelConfig {
  url: string;
  cameraPosition: [number, number, number];
  cameraLookAt: [number, number, number];
  glowColor: string;
  cameraMode: CameraMode;
  splatRotation?: [number, number, number]; // Euler angles in radians
}
```

**`src/systems/ChannelRenderSystem.ts`** — apply it in `createChannelScene` after creating the splat:
```typescript
const splat = new SplatMesh({ url: config.url });
if (config.splatRotation) {
  splat.rotation.set(...config.splatRotation);
}
```

Then per channel in the config, e.g. to flip CH3 upside-down:
```typescript
{
  url: "https://sparkjs.dev/assets/splats/food/iberico-sandwich-by-reserve.spz",
  splatRotation: [Math.PI, 0, 0], // 180° around X = flip upside-down
  ...
}
```

Common rotations:
- `[Math.PI, 0, 0]` — flip upside-down (X axis)
- `[0, Math.PI, 0]` — flip 180° horizontally (Y axis)
- `[0, Math.PI / 2, 0]` — rotate 90° left

Want me to add the field and wire it up so you can just set the numbers in the config?
